From 0f29307795ed29be80febdf0b5e6f2aa14c76e71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 15:08:09 -0500
Subject: panic: flatten nmi_panic control flow

From: Bradley Morgan <brads@mainlining.org>

[ Upstream commit 75eb687ff2bcec9fba31bbe266e5f91e5c283efe ]

panic() is __noreturn, so the else after panic_try_start() is dead.  Drop
it so the force_cpu path can be added cleanly on top.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/20260916182957.7788-3-brads@mainlining.org
Signed-off-by: Bradley Morgan <brads@mainlining.org>
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
Reviewed-by: Petr Mladek <pmladek@suse.com>
Cc: Guenetr Roeck <linux@roeck-us.net>
Cc: Sashiko <sashiko-bot@kernel.org>
Cc: Wang Jinchao <wangjinchao600@gmail.com>
Cc: Wim Van Sebroeck <wim@linux-watchdog.org>
Cc: <stable@vger.kernel.org>
[ sashal: Replaced the missing panic_try_start() and panic_on_other_cpu() helpers with the open-coded old_cpu == PANIC_CPU_INVALID and old_cpu != cpu checks when removing the else. ]
Signed-off-by: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
---
 kernel/panic.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel/panic.c b/kernel/panic.c
index d7973e9754748..3698d2f8c925e 100644
--- a/kernel/panic.c
+++ b/kernel/panic.c
@@ -199,7 +199,8 @@ void nmi_panic(struct pt_regs *regs, const char *msg)
 
 	if (old_cpu == PANIC_CPU_INVALID)
 		panic("%s", msg);
-	else if (old_cpu != cpu)
+
+	if (old_cpu != cpu)
 		nmi_panic_self_stop(regs);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(nmi_panic);
-- 
